{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791563178,"nonce":"/6Cx6P8L2cZKkb3oCQPsCxs8+R4=","title":"Text: measurement, inline runs, and editing primitives","message":"blinc_ts draws single-style text nodes; nothing measures text from TypeScript, and nothing edits it, so no framework can build a text input or a paragraph with a link in it.\n\n**Scope**\n- Measurement: a run's width, line breaks and metrics for a style and width, and the caret positions in it.\n- Inline flow: a paragraph of runs in different styles and elements (spans, links, code), wrapped together, with text-align, as ashui's InlineFlow.\n- Editing primitives for a text field and a text area: caret and selection as data, hit-testing a point to a caret position, word and line movement, selection rects, scrolling the caret into view, IME composition shown in place and the caret rect published to the input method. The input elements themselves are built on these.","files":null}]}